      <data key="d1">"The Good Subarray Problem revolves around identifying subarrays that satisfy the 好数组 condition."&lt;SEP&gt;"好数组 is a subarray defined by two properties: it is not a palindrome, but modifying exactly one element makes it a palindrome. The problem requires counting all such subarrays of a specified length k."&lt;SEP&gt;"好数组 is the computational problem where an array must satisfy two conditions: not being a palindrome, but becoming one after exactly one element modification."&lt;SEP&gt;"好数组 is the problem where an array must satisfy specific properties to be considered good."</data>
